{
 "content": [
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "id you know that we used a stochastic process to generate the CS109 logo? Throw 300,000 darts at a picture of the Stanford seal and only keep the pixels that are hit by at least one dart. Each dart has it's x-pixel and y-pixel chosen independently at random from gaussian distributions:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Let ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "S"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " and be a constant that equals the size of the logo (its width is equal to its height). ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "type": "hardBreak"
    },
    {
     "text": "For the Stanford seal ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "S=300"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ".",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Let ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " be a random variable which represent the x-pixel. ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X \\sim \\mathcal{N}\\left(\\mu = \\frac{S}{2}, \\sigma^2 = (\\frac{S}{2})^2\\right)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Let ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "Y"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " be a random variable which represents the y-pixel.  ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "Y \\sim \\mathcal{N}\\left(\\mu = \\frac{S}{3},\\sigma^2 = (\\frac{S}{5})^2\\right)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "You can re-run the process by pressing the Play animation button:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "sourceBytes": 7122,
    "sourceSha256": "6b08ec918f25154d3e61e496a710c9300bb4935a245cfb718b5bba1c55e6e300"
   },
   "type": "interactive-demo"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Here is the probability density function of ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": "  (left) and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "Y"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " (right) on their own: ",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "sourceBytes": 2509,
    "sourceSha256": "d8a07ccca76287c166e28956750581bcdf510b94594179ba3a195d496986868c"
   },
   "type": "interactive-demo"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Because each dart has an ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "Y"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " value, its location is represented by a joint distribution. Because ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "Y"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " are continuous, we can't represent the joint as a table. ",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Here is a plot the 2D probability density function ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "f(X=x, Y=y)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "sourceBytes": 1701,
    "sourceSha256": "9eee76443a7b2b8653e84d4d0f3bca8dbd649e0787767e7edb98f1fc40ddc0dc"
   },
   "type": "interactive-demo"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "This is a function that has two inputs. The darkness of the color reflects the probability density. ",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Because we know the way the image was created we can reason about some questions:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "bold"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Question: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "What is the probability a dart lands in the center pixel of a canvas that is 300 by 300? ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In other words, what is the probability that ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "150 < X < 151"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "150 < Y < 151"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": "? ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Recall the distributions for ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "Y"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ":",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nX \\sim \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(\\mu_X=\\frac{300}{2},\\;\\sigma_X=\\frac{300}{2}\\right)\\\\\nY \\sim \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(\\mu_Y=\\frac{300}{3},\\;\\sigma_Y=\\frac{300}{5}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Because the two random variables are independent:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\P(&150 < X < 151,\\;\\;  150 < Y < 151)  \\\\\n&=\\P(150 < X < 151) \\cdot \\P(150 < Y < 151)\\\\\n\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Because the two random variables are Gaussian:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nP(150 \\le X \\le 151)\n&=\n\\Phi\\!\\left(\\frac{151 - 150}{150}\\right)\n-\n\\Phi\\!\\left(\\frac{150 - 150}{150}\\right) \\\\\nP(150 \\le Y \\le 151)\n&=\n\\Phi\\!\\left(\\frac{151 - 300}{180}\\right)\n-\n\\Phi\\!\\left(\\frac{150 - 300}{180}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "So if you compute the two numbers and multiply them together you get the probability that a dart hits the center pixel is:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nP(150 \\le X \\le 151,\\;\\; 150 \\le Y \\le 151)\n\\approx 9.4\\times 10^{-6}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "purpleBox"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "bold"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Question: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "What is the probability that if you throw 300,000 darts, no a single dart hits the center pixel? ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Let ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "M"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " be the event that all darts miss the center pixel.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In order for no dart to hit the center pixel, it must be the case that:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "dart 1 misses the center pixel, and",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "dart 2 misses the center pixel, and",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "dart 3 misses the center pixel, and",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "...",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "dart 300,000 misses the center pixel",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Let ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "E_i"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " be the event that dart ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "i"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " misses the center pixel. In the previous problem, we calculated ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "\\P(E_i^C)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ", the probability that a dart hits the center pixel. As such:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\P(E_i) = 1 -  9.4\\times 10^{-6}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Because each dart is independent, the probability of the event ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "M"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ", that no dart hits the center pixel, is the product of the probability of each event ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "E_i"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ":",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\P(M) &= \\prod_{i=1}^{300,000} \\P(E_i)\\\\\n&= \\prod_{i=1}^{300,000} \\big[1 - 9.4\\times 10^{-6}\\big]\\\\\n&=\\big[1 - 9.4\\times 10^{-6}\\big] ^{300000}\\\\\n&\\approx 0.06\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In other words, there is about a 94% chance that the center pixel gets included in the final image!",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "purpleBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "type": "paragraph"
  }
 ],
 "type": "doc"
}
